(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-mystery-11","book":"seventh-wharf","cn":["天亮后，秦衡的[[arrest|逮捕]]问题由办案部门处理，两名清运队人员仍被[[detain|扣留调查]]。工程人员先[[inspect|检查]]C库结构和电气，确认安全才让警员开启钟座。我交出铜钥匙，隔着门看他们把锁扣与外壳[[secure|妥善保全]]。取出的不是操作簿，而是一张油纸包着的旧便条：地下柜十七号，维修纸箱四号。昨夜救出的工人端着热水，看见纸包出来，长长吐了口气。","便条基本[[intact|完整]]，它的编号与已移到高处的箱子相合。警方从箱中[[retrieve|取出]]操作簿，又查港务[[archive|档案]]中的迁库清单和钟的库存照，逐一[[compare|比较]]日期。地下柜只是多年未整理的旧库，锁没有什么神奇机关。赵启所说的藏放经过仍要核对，找到名字并不等于证明全部事实。我望着纸上的开闸签名，终于能忍住不去伸手抢先翻页。","数周后，调查人员给我们看获准公开的对照表。水位记录与操作簿能互相[[confirm|印证]]，旧展文却是[[inconsistent|不一致的]]：它说父亲三点四十分擅自闯航，原簿则记着同一分钟北闸按调度要求开启。这处[[contradiction|矛盾]]接上了三点三十六分的暂缓来电。旧值班员的[[testimony|证言]]又说明，秦衡催的是木材船。十年前展陈借阅登记记着秦衡领走调查录音副本。调查还查到清运队手机中的装音箱指示，设备文件与旧录音的截取段相合；蓝粉与快印社涂层相符，后门水槽也解释了断掉的脚印。","水流复核给出了更[[conclusive|明确有力的]]判断：外河低于港池时提前开闸，水会急速外泄，在七号浮台旁形成强流，是渡船失稳的重要[[cause|原因]]。等水位接近本是常规要求，安全[[failure|失误]]却让赶木材货船的安排压过它。图上把闸门[[operation|操作]]、水位与渡船位置接在一起，没有凭一段录音把每个细节都填满。我终于看懂父亲‘还没回来’那句话，他在替船上的人争几分钟，不是在和水鬼说话。","是否承担[[criminal|刑事的]]责任，还要继续处理，秦衡可以[[deny|否认]]指控，赵启也须回答自己的改写。材料将交[[prosecutor|检察官]]审查，何警官没有提前给我们宣布判决。我过去把[[justice|公正]]想成一声痛快的喊叫，现在它更像一根根必须接牢的缆绳。我拿着公开说明给母亲打电话，没说坏人已经输了，只说：‘他们查到了，爸那天真的要求先别开闸。’电话那头静了一会儿，我听见她把窗关上。"],"en":["By morning, the investigating authorities were handling Qin's [[arrest|arrest]], while the two clearance workers remained subject to procedures to [[detain|detain]] them for investigation. Engineers first had to [[inspect|inspect]] C's structure and electrics. Only after approval did officers open the bell base. I handed over the copper key and watched from the door as they worked to [[secure|secure]] the latch and casing. What emerged was not the register, but an oil-paper-wrapped note: basement cabinet seventeen, maintenance box four. The rescued worker held hot water and let out a long breath when it appeared.","The note was largely [[intact|intact]], and its numbers matched a box already moved uphill. Police could [[retrieve|retrieve]] the register from it, then [[compare|compare]] dates against relocation lists and bell inventory photographs in the port [[archive|archive]]. The basement cabinet was simply old, unsorted storage; its lock had no secret mechanism. Zhao's account of hiding the book still required checking. Finding a name did not establish every fact. Looking at the gate-opening signature, I could finally resist reaching out to turn the page first.","Weeks later, investigators showed us a comparison approved for release. Water readings and the register could [[confirm|confirm]] one another, but the old display was [[inconsistent|inconsistent]] with them: it said Dad forced a passage at 3:40, whereas the original book recorded the gate opening under dispatch orders that same minute. This [[contradiction|contradiction]] connected to his 3:36 call for delay. A former gate officer's [[testimony|testimony]] identified the timber boat as the departure Qin had urged. An exhibition loan entry from ten years earlier recorded Qin collecting an investigation copy of the audio. Police also found speaker-installation messages on a clearance worker's phone. Device files matched an excerpt from the old recording, blue powder matched the shop's coating, and the rear drain explained where the prints had stopped.","The flow review gave a more [[conclusive|conclusive]] finding: opening early when the outer river was lower rapidly drained the basin, creating a strong flow beside Number Seven and an important [[cause|cause]] of the ferry's loss of stability. Waiting for similar water levels was standard. A safety [[failure|failure]] had allowed the hurried timber departure to override it. One diagram connected gate [[operation|operation]], water levels, and the ferry's position, without filling every unknown from a single recording. I finally understood Dad's words, 'My boat isn't back.' He was trying to win minutes for the passengers, not speaking to a water ghost.","Possible [[criminal|criminal]] responsibility still required further proceedings. Qin could [[deny|deny]] the allegations, and Zhao had to answer for his alterations. The material would go to a [[prosecutor|prosecutor]] for review. Officer He announced no verdict in advance. I had imagined [[justice|justice]] as one satisfying shout; now it seemed like ropes that each had to be fastened properly. Holding the public explanation, I called Mum. I did not say the villain had lost. 'They found it,' I said. 'Dad really did ask them not to open the gate.' After a silence, I heard her close the window."]});
